==Old French==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|fro}} {{m|la|tantus}}, {{m|la|tantum}}.

===Adjective===
{{head|fro|adjective|g=m|feminine|tante}}

# [[so much]], [[so many]]

====Declension====
{{fro-decl-adj|ssm=[[tanz]]|opm=tant}}

====Usage notes====
Unlike modern French, ''tant'' can qualify a noun directly without the preposition {{term|de|lang=fro}}:
: '''''tante''' gent'' - so many people

